  "term": "facial nerve",
  "definition": "The facial nerve is the seventh cranial nerve. It includes a larger motor part and a smaller sensory part, helping control facial expression and the tear and salivary glands, while also carrying taste from the front two-thirds of the tongue and touch sensation from the external ear.",
